{"step_index":195,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:25:50Z","content":"NOW I understand the problem! When you log in, NexLev auto-approves and redirects back, but it's going to the dashboard instead of sending the token back to my callback. The OAuth redirect is being swallowed.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach. Let me kill this and do something simpler:","thinking":"I see the problem now. When the OAuth flow redirects to NexLev for authentication, since the user is already logged in, it should auto-approve and redirect back to our callback URL. But instead, it's just going to the NexLev dashboard without redirecting back.\n\nThis means the OAuth flow is not working as expected. The auth endpoint might not be properly handling the redirect. The issue could be:\n\n1. The auth URL parameters aren't being preserved during the redirect\n2. NexLev's OAuth flow might require a specific consent screen that's only shown for certain client IDs\n3. The `chatgpt-mcp-client` client_id might auto-approve without showing a consent screen, but the redirect back to our callback isn't happening\n4. Looking at the browser URL bar in the screenshot, it shows `dashboard.nexlev.io` rather than our localhost callback, confirming the redirect back never actually happened and the user was just dropped onto the NexLev dashboard instead — possibly because this client_id has its own hardcoded redirect behavior.\n\nMaybe the auth server isn't respecting the OAuth redirect parameters and instead defaults to sending logged-in users straight to the dashboard, overriding the callback. I should check the login flow's parameters directly, but it might be faster to just try using Claude Code CLI to make an authenticated NexLev API call, since the user already has it connected there.\n\nActually, Claude Code's authentication is separate from Claude.ai, so that won't help directly. I'm noticing the registered redirect URIs include `http: