{"step_index":227,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:53:23Z","content":"Now I see! The auth endpoint redirects to `/google/authorize` — NexLev uses **Google OAuth** for login. So the flow is:\n\n1. `auth.nexlev.io/authorize` → redirects to Google login\n2. Google login → redirects back to `auth.nexlev.io` \n3. `auth.nexlev.io` → SHOULD redirect to our `localhost:6274/callback` with a code\n\nBut since you're already logged into Google AND NexLev, it auto-completes steps 1-2 and should redirect to step 3. The fact that it's going to the dashboard instead means the redirect is being lost.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach — **intercept the token from your existing Claude.ai connection** instead:","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"# Try the NexLev API endpoint directly - maybe it works with just cookies/session\\n$response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri \\\"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\\\" -Method GET -UseBasicParsing -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue 2>&1\\nWrite-Host \\\"STATUS=$($response.StatusCode)\\\"\\nWrite-Host \\\"CONTENT_TYPE=$($response.Headers.'Content-Type')\\\"\\n$response.Content.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(500, $response.Content.Length))\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"15000","toolAction":"\"Testing MCP endpoint\"","toolSummary":"\"MCP endpoint test\""}}]}
