{"step_index":234,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:54:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T19:24:55+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T19:25:02+05:30\nThe search for \"nexlev API key authentication bearer token alternative to OAuth\" returned the following summary:\nFor the **NexLev API**, you are already using a standard and secure method of authentication: **API Key-based Bearer Token authentication**[1][2].\n\nIf you are looking to understand this method or seek alternatives to the full-scale OAuth flow (which NexLev also supports for specific integrations like AI assistants)[3], here is how these authentication patterns compare and function.\n\n### 1. The Current Method: API Key (Bearer Token)\nNexLev provides an **API Key** that you use as a Bearer Token[1][2]. In technical terms, this is a \"stateless\" credential[4][5].\n*   **How it works:** You include the key in the HTTP header of your requests[6][7].\n    *   **Header format:** `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`[2][7]\n*   **Why it is used:** It is significantly simpler than OAuth[8]. It is ideal for server-to-server communication, n8n workflows, or custom scripts where you do not need to delegate access to a third party[9][2][10].\n*   **Security Tip:** Because it is a \"bearer\" token, anyone who possesses it has access to your account[8][7][5]. **Never share your NexLev API key publicly or commit it to version control**[1][11].\n\n### 2. Alternatives to OAuth\nIf you want to avoid the complexity of OAuth (redirects, authorization servers, etc.) while maintaining secure authentication, here are the standard industry alternatives:\n\n| Method | How it works | Best for... |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **API Key (Current)** | A static or semi-static string passed in the header[7]. | Simple scripts, cron jobs, and internal tools[12]. |\n| **JWT (JSON Web Token)** | A self-contained, signed token that can carry user data[5]. | Stateless applications where you want to embed permissions directly in the token[13][10]. |\n| **Basic Authentication** | Sending `username:password` (Base64 encoded) in the header[8][12]. | **Not recommended** for modern APIs \n<truncated 3074 bytes>\n//vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHDduaNEcrKbnCz7ZPhEwMJvUt_8S5jmxVptYI9lyZ_dGKaTdB72NS0M-o-AowdABr9fr5nDFWfzA1c5tPF0DhETcrEqf04XBSzmjB9XbmcDHVLk-eQGZDpTb1-Ur9QhnfXxislzv1dh1pMd7jtB6VN8Q79HCng3SGZH6QAXNFbGnLQ9BQV1jX3JtDGQkJrwKLUKhMbPu9OiS9931vd2sk9_70LxfRnpKKHfL1CH80=)\n[11] [nexlev.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE0BcicXi7VVbQCBW1VGw0Z1IFre5FRKJdngErJeB85e2Fi-B_iV3nUakn_MiiRaOI4BO4yjl-3htQpasb2d-XjZih1OhMe-sxMf3Nt4VARcjAynLjpXHovQetFTd9nJsZ9Kopr)\n[12] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFRBPqEkkSo-63W4NnK0qnH0uY_8e8wbp3_DQw0Ho48cs7kS_S9iBwEUiXMkLB3tpcTMvfoNnXaEIbA_wHuIim2r2BiXWudMOj4LqNGxnsj6pEj3MU6OsHBoWWxRu9LhaxVTAG13xtYBRmgKqltZyz0aSCJXkIsqPW0HHcJ4pj4rZOcQWWl1dVAGo3MWicqqxfTWgFKcJ1Yr-uwnPO0ekaulrIF4RfxM6RfKthMTDD_xogF23GvPS8OmY48ys5ZLMcALosZ)\n[13] [nordicapis.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFIw_FC4yNLAcwd0YcuRyFQZFHey5NJs4S_VV4-ob1zUCZ2LLGB4jtsqMf_SLdPhSwlVxU5pqj2uNjNFVJyyKr5L7S3d4bnjmnzG8LHNIKkh99X0-cNHZvKvQX2uj2p8EqbE0SMDeG6jGDDy4uu_oqhO-8tng==)\n[14] [echoapi.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGa5Izia-UL3jUPmnqQxEwDC-4BBT-MuGohfRqTW6dy9eZrvM9LlcJT7HniUHqzrrHkkGylJjq60dN1xVn4Kde0wg39suFQ8cE-3FhlyC04ME2XhhWMa8N0gDKcS-bgAA_UC8ZMtM0KLy1e2K-7SQNOV22_jcsU38jirgi8BEFRtTr5GXoQ7xV9cwZa6qfmd-PpRRUfj78k5V8LhADuhV61t90=)\n[15] [loginradius.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFrEDTlXsW4tB9XclZvuUKdq4vKHNKLwOsXkF7pycBfWH3XAOWaFiyotwN9mh1KTpslPHhSGzbh9dneq6ZcjW4G-BoFSa_SXUR4cPGskMM5ndX2DHb-2h69ki5aLHY11CwVzTLkhN75DTt-0l2VLhlkBI4j4ylkFxH8Lz528JthUKYu-W1okgm8hA3AE3jyP5LY)\n[16] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.googl